 "notes": "Light-shining-through-wall (Primakoff in Ge crystals) search at EuXFEL; no DM density assumption. Headline curve = pink 'EuXFEL' region boundary of Fig. 5 (bounds.png from e-print), digitised via pixel analysis with axis calibration from tick marks (x: 1e-3 to 1e4 eV, y: 1e-1 to ~5e-5 GeV^-1, log-log). Broadband on-Bragg bound is flat at ~5.1e-4 GeV^-1 from 1e-3 eV up to ~30 eV, rising steeply near the Ge plasma frequency (44 eV) and cut off at ~46 eV (closed at plot top 1e-1). Four narrow off-Bragg lines (Delta m_a ~ 1e-3 eV per paper; width exaggerated in Fig. 5) at m_a = 340, 460, 1100, 2400 eV are represented as narrow spikes (mass +/-0.1%) down to the plotted tips 4.07e-4, 4.98e-4, 4.70e-4, 3.53e-4 GeV^-1. Note: Table I quotes g_agamma = 3.91e-4 (on-Bragg, m_a <~44 eV) and 3.10e-4, 3.87e-4, 3.69e-4, 2.76e-4 GeV^-1 for the four off-Bragg masses, uniformly ~1.29x below the plotted Fig. 5 curve; the figure was traced as the headline presentation. 90% CL (N_det = 2.3 events, zero observed).",
